<title>ARGENTINA: Argentine Central Bank reserves detailed.</title>
<headline>Argentine Central Bank reserves detailed.</headline>
<dateline>BUENOS AIRES 1996-10-24</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Argentine Central Bank Thursday released the following international reserve and currency liability data, in millions:</p>
<p>*A = International reserves (gold, currency, securities, including repos and reverse repos).</p>
<p>B = Liquidity requirements.</p>
<p>C = International reserves in the financial system.</p>
<p>*D = Monetary base.</p>
<p>E = Currency liabilities.</p>
<p>F = Net repurchase tender agreements.</p>
<p>G = Bank liquidity paper.</p>
<p>H = Financial liabilities.</p>
<p>   Date	*A*   *B*    *C*    *D*    *E*   *F*   *G*    *H*</p>
<p>  Oct 11  19,294 3,568 22,862 12,478 12,512 4,201   614 18,001</p>
<p>  Oct 14  19,289 3,568 22,857 12,324 12,358 4,644   614 17,973</p>
<p>  Oct 15  18,981 3,689 22,670 12,254 12,288 4,505   614 17,679</p>
<p>  Oct 16  18,670 3,766 22,436 12,169 12,203 4,333   589 17,359</p>
<p>  Oct 17  18,479 3,744 22,223 12,134 12,168 4,418   589 17,185</p>
<p>  Oct 18  18,981 3,666 22,647 12,122 12,156 4,543   589 17,683</p>
<p>  Oct 21  18,876 3,708 22,584 12,080 12,114 4,560   589 17,557</p>
<p>  Oct 22  18,814 3,736 22,550 11,933 11,941 4,672   589 17,496</p>
<p>*A  Of the $18.81 billion in international reserves, $2.68 billion (14.23 percent) are in securities.</p>
<p>*D  There are currently no peso-denominated current accounts at the Central Bank.</p>
<p>-- Buenos Aires Newsroom +54 1 318-0652</p>
</text>
